message: "If you use or adapt this resource, please cite it as below."
title: "Miller & Bragg: Interactive Crystallography from Miller Indices to X-ray Diffraction"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Peter
    family-names: Nockemann
    affiliation: "Queen's University Belfast, UK"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9864-9702"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, single-file teaching tool for Miller indices and X-ray
  diffraction, for undergraduate and taught postgraduate courses in chemistry,
  materials science, physics and engineering. It draws the section of any
  lattice plane inside a unit cell, takes students through indexing one step
  at a time, generates matching exercises, question banks for Canvas and
  Moodle and printable worksheets, covers tetragonal, orthorhombic and
  hexagonal (Miller-Bravais) cells, and links planes to diffraction: a Bragg's
  law simulator with a simulated powder pattern, a powder-indexing exercise,
  and single-crystal diffraction with the Ewald construction and rotation
  photographs. It runs offline in any browser and needs no installation.
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - Miller indices
  - X-ray diffraction
  - Bragg's law
  - Ewald sphere
  - powder diffraction
  - chemistry education
  - materials science education
